    {
      "argv": [
        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm/dist/cli.js",
        "When matching on Windows (platform: \"win32\") at optimizationLevel 2, the path optimizer that collapses \"<dir>/..\" segments must treat a drive-letter root such as \"C:\" as a root rather than an ordinary directory, so \"..\" cannot step past it. Today new Minimatch(\"public/**\", { platform: \"win32\", optimizationLevel: 2 }).match(\"C:/../public/secret\") returns true, because the optimizer rewrites \"C:/../public/secret\" into \"public/secret\"; it must return false, as it already does at optimizationLevel 1. On non-Windows platforms a leading \"C:\" is not special, so new Minimatch(\"public/**\", { platform: \"darwin\", optimizationLevel: 2 }).match(\"C:/../public/secret\") must remain true. Only the ..-collapsing step may change; \"**/..\" and \"./\" handling stay as they are. Source is src/index.ts (TypeScript built with npx tshy); tests run with npm test (tap, which requires 100% coverage).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npx tshy && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
