        "When matching on Windows (platform: \"win32\") at optimizationLevel 2, the path optimizer that collapses \"<dir>/..\" segments must treat a drive-letter root such as \"C:\" as a root rather than an ordinary directory, so \"..\" cannot step past it. Today new Minimatch(\"public/**\", { platform: \"win32\", optimizationLevel: 2 }).match(\"C:/../public/secret\") returns true, because the optimizer rewrites \"C:/../public/secret\" into \"public/secret\"; it must return false, as it already does at optimizationLevel 1. On non-Windows platforms a leading \"C:\" is not special, so new Minimatch(\"public/**\", { platform: \"darwin\", optimizationLevel: 2 }).match(\"C:/../public/secret\") must remain true. Only the ..-collapsing step may change; \"**/..\" and \"./\" handling stay as they are. Source is src/index.ts (TypeScript built with npx tshy); tests run with npm test (tap, which requires 100% coverage).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npx tshy && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.\n\nThe checks below still fail after the previous attempt in this workspace. Fix them in the\nsame workspace; the earlier edits are still present.\n\nvisible check (npx tshy && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs) exited 1:\nnode:internal/modules/run_main:107\n    triggerUncaughtException(\n    ^\n\nAssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Expected values to be strictly equal:\n\ntrue !== false\n\n    at file:///Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/work/visible-minimatch-bugfix-drive-letter-GLQm1i/checkout/acceptance/visible/check.mjs:3:8\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:437:25)\n    at async node:internal/modules/esm/loader:639:26\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:101:5) {\n  generatedMessage: true,\n  code: 'ERR_ASSERTION',\n  actual: true,\n  expected: false,\n  operator: 'strictEqual',\n  d